Inflow control devices (ICDs) are completion components installed in oil and gas wells to regulate fluid entry along the wellbore. By helping distribute inflow more evenly, they can reduce premature water or gas breakthrough associated with uneven formation pressure and improve production management.

Demand is supported by horizontal well development, complex reservoir conditions, and the need to improve recovery from existing fields. Autonomous inflow control devices are also gaining attention because they can respond to changing fluid conditions and help manage unwanted water or gas production.

